<title>BELGIUM: EU says clears buy of Stinnes coal unit.</title>
<headline>EU says clears buy of Stinnes coal unit.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said in a statement on Tuesday it had cleared the control by Rheinbraun Brennstoff GmbH and SHV Energy NV of the hard coal trading activities of Stinnes AG.</p>
<p>It said that the joint venture to be created as a result of the acquisition of Stinnes Intercoal &quot;would not give any power to the parties to increase prices&quot; or to impede fair competition in the European market.</p>
<p>Stinnes Intercoal currently belongs to the German Veba group which is also the largest shareholder in Ruhrkohle, another German producer and trader of coal. Rheinbraun is ultimately controlled by German electricity group RWE.</p>
<p>The deal was cleared under the rules governing the European Coal and Steel Community.</p>
</text>
